{
  "method": {
    "overhead": "per boundary, interleaved pairs of the same call bare and recorded (order alternating within a pair), timed with time.perf_counter_ns; overhead = median and p95 of the paired differences (recorded - bare), next to the median and p95 of each side; calls run in sessions of `batch` calls after `warmup` discarded pairs; GC enabled",
    "session": "the fixed cost of one recording session with no calls (create, enter, exit, finish), median and p95 over iterations / batch sessions",
    "replay_served": "each recorded session replayed in full mode; the time of every served call (lookup, fingerprint, decode), median and p95",
    "append": "the recorded call in sessions of `batch` calls kept in memory and in sessions also appending each envelope to <out>.partial, alternating which goes first; overhead = median of (appended - in memory) paired by call index; finish() timed for both; the worst boundary's overhead over the median latency_ms of the live suite's model envelopes",
    "recorded_live_ms": "sum of the cassette's envelope latency_ms (the agent calls one boundary at a time); excludes the agent's own code between calls, so it is a lower bound on the live run's wall-clock",
    "replay_ms": "wall-clock of agent_replay.ci.run_scenario (load cassette and agent, full replay; with or without the suite's checks, judge from its committed cache), median of `repeats` runs after one warm-up; speedup = recorded_live_ms / median"
  },
